  "title": "Top Quartile Test Kits by Result Turnaround",
  "prompt": "You manage an at-home diagnostic test kit platform. Each kit ships to a patient, who completes the test and mails it back to the lab. The lab then releases the results. You need to identify the test kits with the fastest turnaround times (from shipment to result release) to recognize high-performing lab batches. Write a query that returns the top 25% (top quartile) of test kits ranked by their turnaround time in hours, from fastest to slowest. Turnaround time is calculated as the number of hours between `shipped_at` and `result_released_at`. If multiple kits have the same turnaround time at the 25% boundary, include all tied kits (use PERCENT_RANK so ties at the boundary are included). Your output must include four columns: `kit_id`, `patient_email`, `turnaround_hours`, and `percent_rank_value` (the PERCENT_RANK score rounded to 4 decimal places). Order the results by `turnaround_hours` ASC, then by `kit_id` ASC for ties.",
